## Full Eternity Band as a Wedding Band

The full eternity band puts emerald cut diamonds all the way around the ring, not just across the top half. The [3ct tw H-I/SI1-SI2 in 14K white gold](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/emerald-cut-diamond-eternity-ring-in-14k-white-gold-3-ct-tw-h-i-si1-si2-item-257650?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is currently [$6,435](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/emerald-cut-diamond-eternity-ring-in-14k-white-gold-3-ct-tw-h-i-si1-si2-item-257650?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) on 25% sale from $8,580 — the most reviewed emerald cut diamond wedding band in certified inventory at 45 reviews.

The eternity differs from the seven-stone in one key way: diamonds go all the way around. More total stones. More diamond exposure from every angle.

More clarity risk — the H-I/SI1-SI2 grade range carries the same SI2 variability as any natural step-cut band, and more stones means more individual tables to assess.

The trade-offs against the seven-stone are worth knowing. Full eternity bands cannot be resized by the conventional method — the stones go all the way around, so sizing requires removing and resetting stones. Confirm your ring size before purchasing.

At $6,435 for 3ct total weight with 45 confirmed reviews, the full eternity is the highest-value, most-tested option in this format. The seven-stone at $2,962 gives you less diamond for less money. The eternity at $6,435 gives you a full-circle statement band at twice the price.

