## How to Pair a Plain Diamond Band With an Emerald Cut Ring

If you want a wedding band that doesn't feature emerald cut diamonds — a plain diamond band, a pave band, or a simple metal band — specific choices reduce the gap problem significantly.

A thin straight-shank band minimizes the gap. Look for a band under 2mm wide with a flat inner face. Comfort-fit bands have a rounded inner surface that creates more gap than a traditional-fit band.

Traditional-fit (flat inside) presses closer to the solitaire's base.

A plain metal band in the same metal creates the cleanest stack. No diamonds competing with the solitaire. No prongs catching or migrating.

The plain band becomes a frame for the emerald cut — invisible until you look at the pair from the side.

A slender pave band under 2mm can work if the profile is low. Avoid channel-set bands, which have raised metal rails that create their own gap. Avoid any band with a dome profile.

[![Emerald diamond wedding band lifestyle](/images/602390_Y_1_1600X1600.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/double-emerald-diamond-wedding-ring-in-18k-yellow-gold-4-mm-1-8-ct-tw-item-194925?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

